# Code owners.
#
# The v5.0 charter (§25) requires named Security, Privacy/Compliance and
# Principal Engineering sign-off before Phase 1 work begins, and §5 asks who is
# accountable for each feature. Neither existed, so every row of the audit's
# Feature Reality Matrix read `unassigned`.
#
# The honest answer is that this repository has one contributor — 99 of 99
# commits — and that all three roles collapse onto that person. §25 states
# explicitly that this is a legitimate answer. What is not legitimate is
# leaving the roles nominally unfilled, because that turns an accepted risk
# into an unnoticed one: a reader assumes somebody is reviewing security, and
# nobody is.
#
# So this file records reality rather than an aspiration. When a second
# contributor joins, the security-sensitive paths below should move to them, so
# that no single person both writes and approves changes to the encryption
# boundary.

* @Fskalony

